        "subject": "LU-20399 o2iblnd: determine FastReg gaps correctly",
        "message": "LU-20399 o2iblnd: determine FastReg gaps correctly\n\nkiblnd_setup_rd_kiov() sets tx->tx_gaps when a bulk transfer cannot be\ndescribed by a single page-aligned memory region, so the gapped case\ncan be diverted (or preemptively rejected on devices without FastReg\ngaps support) instead of being handed to ib_map_mr_sg(), which would\nshort-map the scatterlist and fail registration with -EINVAL.\n\nThe gap test has been dead since it was introduced. fragnob is\nmin(bv_len - offset, nob), so \"fragnob < bv_len - offset\" is true only\nwhen nob is the smaller term, in which case fragnob == nob and\n\"nob > fragnob\" is false. The two conditions are mutually exclusive,\nso tx_gaps was never set and every gapped transfer fell through to\nib_map_mr_sg().\n\nReplace the test with the actual gap condition, mirroring the kernel's\nib_sg_to_pages(): a non-first fragment that starts mid-page, or a\nnon-last fragment that ends mid-page, introduces a gap. The first\nfragment's start offset and the last fragment's end offset remain\nexempt. This now flags the two-fragment case above, where the first\nfragment ends mid-page.\n\nThis does not by itself make a gapped transfer succeed on a device\nwithout gaps support; it restores the intended diversion and the\npreemptive -EPROTONOSUPPORT path with its actionable message rather\nthan a bare short-map -EINVAL.\n\nFixes: e40ea6fd4494 (\"LU-11064 lnd: determine gaps correctly\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I70a6a92a4428a93a1bfac979a3c7d822e7973bad\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66689\nReviewed-by: Manish Regmi <mregmi@ddn.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Cyril Bordage <cbordage@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Xinxia Qu <xqu@ddn.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
